/ref 17592186045453 13194139535590 true] [17592186356527 1111 #uuid "3614ff9a-665c-56c4-8cec-6fe5af2263e8" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356528 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535590 true] [17592186356528 1111 #uuid "a11d53c4-3de2-53fd-a739-2028f19c29fc" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356529 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535590 true] [17592186356529 1111 #uuid "d0a592d0-06a5-5e5d-be23-a0f836c6a23b" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356531 13194139535590 true] [17592186356530 1089 "q-81702" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535590 true] [17592186356530 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/assets/cb5c201068966a7d25ff3640d478e03a78bc075900181bdee93d5612b0217609.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356530 1113 #uuid "e7e83189-ee56-5f10-ab1d-ea1635f00e48" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356530 1145 "Notice that $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix. So, we need to find its scale factor and the angle of rotation.\n\nWe can find the scale factor using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent $A$ as a product of a rotation and a scaling matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =3[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$  and scale the result by a scale factor of $3,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/assets/7165c52d2280e4a53dc640acdca7671dcb897921028e675a583c46e6ccd40e33.png)" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356532 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356533 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356534 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356535 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356536 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1041 "selection" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356533 13194139535590 true] [17592186356531 1110 #uuid "b4932b46-e40b-53d8-979f-564ea830c7b3" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356532 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/assets/f8687f4701d12d4d30d10d2164c5a9870c1c6681324e995ce14a01612f36f2d6.png" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535590 true] [17592186356532 1111 #uuid "771f570b-ed79-5278-af47-eae018af033c" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356533 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/assets/fe595c5a2139ece74e7158ffa6374a5757e4bfd0f3c0427edd88a7ffba7c6bff.png" 13194139535590 true] [17592186356533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186